.\" Manpage for append_path
.TH append_path 1 "October 26, 2026" "202610261214-git" "append_path"

.SH NAME
append_path

.SH DESCRIPTION
Add directories to the current shell's PATH. Dot-source the script to define the function in the current shell. Running it directly with directory arguments exits with status 64 because a child process cannot modify its parent shell's environment.

.SH SYNOPSIS
\. /path/to/append_path
.br
append_path [options] [directory ...]
.br
/path/to/append_path --completions short|long

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Display the full help.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Display current version.
.TP
.B \-\-options
List supported options.
.TP
.B \-\-completions short|long
List the short or long completion values.
.TP
.B \-\-silent
Suppress status output. This is the default.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Show status output.
.TP
.B \-\-
Treat remaining arguments as directory paths.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B . /usr/local/bin/append_path
Load the append_path function into the current shell.
.TP
.B append_path --verbose /usr/bin/site_perl
Add a directory to the current shell's PATH and show status.
.TP
.B /usr/local/bin/append_path /path/to/dir
Fails with a source-required message.
.TP
.B /usr/local/bin/append_path --completions long
Print supported long options.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B APPEND_PATH_SILENT
Set to "true" to suppress status output by default, or "false" to show it. The --silent and --verbose options override this value.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I
/usr/local/bin/append_path

